@@ -120,3 +120,42 @@ validates prospective native replacements locally.
 Platform services (threads, virtual memory, plugins, files, clocks) go through
 `platform/os.h`, with POSIX and Win32 implementations; the build is
 CMake with presets per platform (`CMakePresets.json`).
+
+## Browser DirectPlay transport
+
+`dx/directplay.cpp` adapts the DirectPlay 4 ANSI and Lobby 3 ANSI COM layouts to
+an ordered binary WebSocket room protocol. Session/player state, payload queues
+and relative pointer relocation metadata are owned host values. Guest pointers
+are validated/copied only during COM calls holding the scheduler baton. Guest
+callbacks get transient guest allocations, never host pointers. Provider release
+unregisters notification before closing its socket.
+
+`platform/os.h` exposes bounded binary WebSockets and notification registration.
+The browser callback queues bytes and signals the registered guest event through
+`guest_event_signal_from_host`; it never decodes packets or calls guest code.
+RPC waits use `guest_sleep_ms` to release the baton. Draining, HRESULT handling,
+system-message construction and pointer relocation happen on the guest thread.
+An injectable `DirectPlayTransport` supports native contract tests through the
+same COM dispatch paths and cannot be replaced while provider objects exist.
+Queued binary input and DirectPlay messages retain 2 MiB byte budgets and
+4096-entry limits; pending async send completions also have a 4096-entry limit.
+The larger count budget supports small-chunk transfer bursts without removing
+the byte bound. It does not supply receiver-consumption backpressure. Browser
+input rejection closes with application code 4009, because client close calls
+cannot use the server's 1009 message-too-large code.
+
+The relay routes unchanged game packets, owns room/player identities and enforces
+per-connection sequence numbers. Async SendEx completes only after relay enqueue
+acceptance, not after another simulation consumes the command. Size negotiation
+and peek retain the original message until successful removal. Malformed input,
+sequence gaps, bounded-queue overflow or transport failure queue session loss;
+there is no reconnect replay. Unsupported DirectPlay APIs still fail explicitly.
+
+The web launcher stages an engine SHA-256 and hashes actual imported content
+paths/bytes before launching. Writable profiles and generated viewport overlays
+are separate. `RECOMP_NETWORK_URL` chooses the room service and the launcher
+sets `RECOMP_NETWORK_MANIFEST`; URL parameters cannot spoof that manifest.
+Named profiles permit two browser instances to share imported immutable data.
+Optional visible network diagnostics receive the game's native stderr output;
+session loss always offers launcher/reload recovery, including with diagnostics
+closed. This transport does not confer simulation authority or cheat resistance.
